## 8. Deployment Requirements (AWS EC2)
- OS: Ubuntu 22.04 LTS EC2 instance (t2.micro is sufficient)
- Security group: inbound 22 (SSH, restricted to agent/user IP if known), 80 (HTTP)
- Install: Python 3, pip, venv, Nginx
- App runs under Gunicorn, managed by a systemd service (auto-restart on crash/reboot)
- Nginx reverse-proxies port 80 → Gunicorn on 127.0.0.1:8000
- Final deliverable: a public IP/URL where the live app is reachable
- `README.md` must document exact steps taken so they're reproducible manually

## 9. Success Criteria
- [ ] Model trains and achieves reasonable R² (>0.7 on synthetic data) — printed/logged
- [ ] `/api/predict` returns correct JSON shape and sane values for boundary inputs (0s, max values)
- [ ] Frontend loads, sliders work, prediction + chart update on submit, no console errors
- [ ] App runs locally via `python app.py` or gunicorn without errors
- [ ] App is reachable over the public internet on the EC2 instance's IP on port 80
- [ ] `GET /api/health` returns 200 from the public URL
- [ ] Code pushed to a GitHub repo with a clear README